{#
    THE product card — one definition for the whole theme.

    The card is the platform's own <falak-product-card>, which is what the home
    rows already render through <falak-products-list> and
    <falak-products-slider>. This partial exists so the server-rendered pages
    (listing, search, brand, wishlist) render the SAME element rather than a
    second copy of the markup — the theme had two cards before, and the same
    product wore a different one depending on where a shopper found it.

    The record is handed over as a JSON attribute because these pages already
    have it from the server; the element therefore paints without a fetch.

        {% include 'pages.partials.product-card' %}

    | product | object | a record already in hand (listing, search, brand…) |
    | source  | string | analytics label; defaults to the enclosing page     |
#}
{# show-add-button / show-wishlist are opt-in on the component: the home
   rows switch them on through <falak-products-list card-button card-wishlist>,
   so a card placed here has to ask for them too or it renders with no way to
   buy and no heart. #}
<falak-product-card
    product="{{ product|json_encode|escape('html_attr') }}"
    show-add-button
    show-wishlist
    source="{{ source|default('listing') }}"></falak-product-card>
